-- title:
--   U_λ-eigenvalue on Hecke eigenvectors in the Tate module
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive integer and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the sense of the project: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity on coprime indices and the usual prime-power recursions, with the split recursion at primes dividing the level) and for no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ does there exist a normalised eigenform of level $M'$ whose coefficients at the primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals with $\lambda\notin S$ and $\lambda\mid M$. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{T}=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(M)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M$, $q\notin S$, to $\mathbb{C}$, with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$. Let $O''$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, $K$ a field of characteristic zero which is an $O''$-algebra, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $K$. Equip $J_0(M)=\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with the module structure over the abstract Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[X_p : p \text{ prime}]$ given by [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82), and let $T_\lambda(J_0(M))$ be the submodule of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\,x_{n+1}=x_n$. The assertion is then: for every $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T_\lambda(J_0(M))$ for which $(a\cdot x)_n=(a \bmod \lambda^n)\,x_n$, every ring homomorphism $TM$ from the abstract Hecke algebra to $\operatorname{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T_\lambda(J_0(M)))$ acting on pure tensors by $t\mapsto (a\otimes x\mapsto a\otimes t\cdot x)$, and every $v\in K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T_\lambda(J_0(M)))$, if the base change to $K$ of $TM(X_\ell)$ sends $v$ to $\varphi(\chi_g(T_\ell))\,v$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, then the base change of $TM(X_\lambda)$ sends $v$ to $\varphi(\chi_g(U_\lambda))\,v$.
--
--   This is the statement that a common eigenvector for the Hecke operators away from the level, inside the $\lambda$-adic Tate module of $J_0(M)$ base changed to $K$, is automatically an eigenvector for the operator at the prime $\lambda\mid M$, with the eigenvalue prescribed by the newform $g$; it is the Tate-module counterpart of the fact that a newform is an eigenform for the full Hecke algebra. It is used in the construction of the two-dimensional Hecke-pinned eigenplane in the Tate module, [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_heckePinnedEigenPlane_tateModule_jZero`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_heckePinnedEigenPlane_tateModule_jZero).
